<title>SPAIN: CYCLING-BOARDMAN WINS TOUR OF CATALONIA TIME TRIAL.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-BOARDMAN WINS TOUR OF CATALONIA TIME TRIAL.</headline>
<dateline>VILA SECA, Spain 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>British time-trial specialist Chris Boardman led the Tour of Catalonia after Thursday's two-part opening stage.</p>
<p>Boardman won the eight-km time trial in eight minutes 42 seconds -- 12 seconds faster than Spaniards Angel Luis Casero and Aitor Garmendia who were second and third respectively.</p>
<p>Earlier, Jan Svorada of Slovakia won a sprint finish to the 72-km leg from Vila Seca to La Pineda in one hour 57 minutes 23 seconds.</p>
</text>
